5:39:48 PM [express] GET /api/lessons/c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415 200 in 5ms :: {"id":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","title":"The Arabic Letter System","titleAr":"نظام الحروف العربية","description":"Discover how Arabic letters change shape based on their position in a word. Learn the 4 forms: isolated, initial, medial, and final — starting with Alif (أ), Ba (ب), Ta (ت), and Tha (ث).","descriptionAr":"اكتشف كيف تتغير أشكال الحروف العربية حسب موقعها في الكلمة. تعلّم الأشكال الأربعة: المنفرد، البداية، الوسط، والنهاية","level":1,"orderIndex":1,"category":"alphabet","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":60,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Low","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Recognize all 28 Arabic letters in their isolated forms","Identify letter families by shared base shapes","Distinguish letters by their dot patterns","Write basic letter shapes with correct stroke direction","Pronounce each letter with its correct sound"],"canDoStatements":["I can recognize Arabic letters when I see them","I can name the 28 letters of the Arabic alphabet","I can write individual Arabic letters","I can pronounce each letter's basic sound"],"prerequisites":[],"estimatedMinutes":25}
5:39:48 PM [express] GET /api/lessons/c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415/exercises 200 in 19ms :: [{"id":"f4a6a517-10e3-471b-9618-3e233a2ccd60","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Arabic letters change shape based on their position. How many forms does each letter have?","questionAr":"الحروف العربية تتغير حسب موقعها. كم شكلاً لكل حرف؟","context":"Unlike English where 'a' always looks the same, Arabic letters like ب can look like بـ ـبـ ـب depending on where they appear in a word.","contextAr":"على عكس الإنجليزية، الحروف العربية مثل ب تتغير شكلها حسب موقعها في الكلمة","hint":"Think about it: isolated, start of word, middle of word, end of word","hintAr":null,"options":["2 forms","3 forms","4 forms","5 forms"],"correctAnswer":"4 forms","explanation":"Each Arabic letter has 4 forms: isolated (ب), initial (بـ), medial (ـبـ), and final (ـب). This is because Arabic is written in connected script.","explanationAr":"لكل حرف ٤ أشكال: منفرد (ب)، بداية (بـ)، وسط (ـبـ)، نهاية (ـب)","grammarNote":"Some letters like أ (Alif), د (Dal), ذ (Dhal), ر (Ra), ز (Zay), و (Waw) only connect from the right side, so they only have 2 distinct forms.","grammarNoteAr":"بعض الحروف مثل أ، د، ذ، ر، ز، و تتصل من اليمين فقط، لذا لها شكلان فقط","skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":1},{"id":"8d1890fd-8ffa-4d7e-910c-e63b6682df09","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Look at these letters: ب ت ث ن — they share the same base shape. What makes them different?","questionAr":"انظر إلى هذه الحروف: ب ت ث ن — لها نفس الشكل الأساسي. ما الذي يميزها؟","context":"Arabic uses a brilliant system: many letters share the same base shape but are distinguished by dots (نُقَط). This means fewer shapes to memorize!","contextAr":"تستخدم العربية نظاماً ذكياً: حروف كثيرة تشترك في الشكل الأساسي وتتميز بالنقط","hint":"Count the dots and notice where they are placed — above or below the base shape","hintAr":null,"options":["Their size","The number and position of dots","Their color","The direction they face"],"correctAnswer":"The number and position of dots","explanation":"ب has 1 dot below, ت has 2 dots above, ث has 3 dots above, ن has 1 dot above. This dot system is a key feature of Arabic script.","explanationAr":"ب لها نقطة تحت، ت لها نقطتان فوق، ث لها ٣ نقط فوق، ن لها نقطة فوق","grammarNote":"The base shape of ب ت ث ن is called a 'tooth' (سِنّ) in Arabic calligraphy. Once you learn this shape, you know 4 letters!","grammarNoteAr":"الشكل الأساسي لـ ب ت ث ن يسمى 'سِنّ' في الخط العربي. تعلّم شكلاً واحداً واعرف ٤ حروف!","skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":2},{"id":"6d8409a2-88dc-4284-b9cf-ea11ec655c5f","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Which letter is Alif (أ)? It's the first letter and looks like a vertical stroke.","questionAr":"أي حرف هو الألف؟ إنه الحرف الأول ويبدو كخط عمودي","context":"Alif is special — it's the only letter that doesn't connect to the letter after it. It represents the glottal stop sound (like the pause in 'uh-oh').","contextAr":"الألف حرف مميز — لا يتصل بالحرف الذي بعده. يمثل صوت الهمزة","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ب","أ","ت","ع"],"correctAnswer":"أ","explanation":"Alif (أ) looks like a vertical line ا. It's unique because it carries vowels (fatha, kasra, damma) but doesn't have its own consonant sound.","explanationAr":"الألف تبدو كخط عمودي ا. مميزة لأنها تحمل الحركات لكن ليس لها صوت ساكن خاص","grammarNote":"Alif can carry hamza (أ إ) or stand alone as a long vowel (ا). In 'باب' (door), the second Alif is a long 'aa' sound.","grammarNoteAr":"الألف تحمل الهمزة (أ إ) أو تقف وحدها كحرف مد. في 'باب'، الألف الثانية هي مد بالألف","skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":3},{"id":"43018aef-2a98-4a66-b17e-81b0cfddc4bd","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"fill_blank","difficulty":1,"question":"The letter ب (Ba) has one dot ___ the base shape","questionAr":"حرف ب (الباء) له نقطة واحدة ___ الشكل الأساسي","context":"The position of dots — above or below — is critical for reading Arabic correctly.","contextAr":null,"hint":"Look carefully at ب — is the dot above or below?","hintAr":"انظر بعناية إلى ب — هل النقطة فوق أم تحت؟","options":null,"correctAnswer":"below","explanation":"Ba (ب) has one dot BELOW. Compare: ب (below=Ba), ت (2 above=Ta), ث (3 above=Tha), ن (1 above=Nun).","explanationAr":"الباء لها نقطة تحت. قارن: ب (تحت=باء)، ت (فوق=تاء)، ث (٣ فوق=ثاء)، ن (فوق=نون)","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":4},{"id":"968032e8-7b69-4242-acbf-9e357e87e68f","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"sentence_order","difficulty":1,"question":"Put these letters in Arabic alphabetical order (أبجدية):","questionAr":"رتّب هذه الحروف حسب الترتيب الأبجدي:","context":"The Arabic alphabet has 28 letters. The first four are: Alif, Ba, Ta, Tha. Notice how Ba, Ta, Tha share a base shape with different dots.","contextAr":"الأبجدية العربية فيها ٢٨ حرفاً. الأربعة الأوائل: ألف، باء، تاء، ثاء","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ت","ب","ث","أ"],"correctAnswer":"أ ب ت ث","explanation":"The correct order is أ ب ت ث (Alif, Ba, Ta, Tha). This is the start of the modern Arabic alphabet order used in dictionaries.","explanationAr":"الترتيب الصحيح: أ ب ت ث — بداية الترتيب الأبجدي المستخدم في القواميس","grammarNote":"Arabic actually has TWO ordering systems: the modern alphabet (أبجدية) used in dictionaries, and the older Abjadi order (أبجدهوز) used for numbering.","grammarNoteAr":"للعربية نظامان: الترتيب الحديث (الأبجدي) للقواميس، والترتيب القديم (الأبجدي الحسابي) للترقيم","skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":5},{"id":"8238beff-a5fc-4602-90eb-839c7979339b","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Which word contains the letter ب (Ba)?","questionAr":"أي كلمة تحتوي على حرف ب (الباء)؟","context":"Now practice spotting letters inside real words. Remember, ب might look different when connected: بـ ـبـ ـب","contextAr":"تدرّب الآن على إيجاد الحروف داخل كلمات حقيقية. تذكر أن ب تتغير عند الاتصال","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["تَمْر (dates)","بَاب (door)","ثَلْج (snow)","نَار (fire)"],"correctAnswer":"بَاب (door)","explanation":"بَاب (baab = door) contains ب twice! In initial position (بـ) and in final position (ـب). The word literally has the pattern: Ba-Alif-Ba.","explanationAr":"بَاب (باب = door) تحتوي على ب مرتين! في البداية وفي النهاية","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":6},{"id":"4c465257-81ea-43e0-8c8d-b636d2cbc2ad","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"In the word بِنْت (bint = girl), the letter ب appears in which position?","questionAr":"في كلمة بِنْت، حرف ب يظهر في أي موضع؟","context":"Remember the 4 positions: isolated (standalone), initial (start of word), medial (middle), final (end).","contextAr":"تذكر المواضع الأربعة: منفرد، بداية، وسط، نهاية","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Isolated","Initial (start)","Medial (middle)","Final (end)"],"correctAnswer":"Initial (start)","explanation":"In بِنْت, the ب is at the beginning of the word, so it's in the initial position (بـ). It connects to the ن after it.","explanationAr":"في بِنْت، الباء في بداية الكلمة، فهي في الموضع الابتدائي وتتصل بالنون بعدها","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":7},{"id":"889fa218-0110-428c-8201-1116dc454edd","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"fill_blank","difficulty":2,"question":"Complete the Arabic alphabet sequence: أ ب ت ___","questionAr":"أكمل تسلسل الأبجدية العربية: أ ب ت ___","context":null,"contextAr":null,"hint":"It looks like ت but with three dots instead of two","hintAr":"تبدو مثل ت لكن بثلاث نقط بدلاً من اثنتين","options":null,"correctAnswer":"ث","explanation":"ث (Tha) comes after ت (Ta). It has 3 dots above the same base shape. Think of it as 'Ta with an extra dot' = Tha.","explanationAr":"ث (ثاء) تأتي بعد ت (تاء). لها ٣ نقط فوق نفس الشكل الأساسي","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"writing","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":8}]
